#N canvas 60 60 1000 820 10;
#X text 30 10 f.util.guiinhibit -- stops the patch echoing a parameter back to the GUI while the player's finger is on that parameter's widget. \$1 = the safety timeout in ms.;
#X text 30 48 Why. A widget the player is dragging was being repainted mid-drag by the engine's own echo on the same address. Open Stage Control's native widgets defer an incoming value while they are touched (setValueTouchedQueue) and apply it on release \, so they were protected \; formuls' own slider canvases draw themselves and are not \, so they jittered. Measured over two logged sessions \, canvas widgets showed a mean of 2.65 displayed reversals per touch against a finger mean of 0.08 -- a 33x inflation \, all of it echo. Suppressing at the source also keeps the needless traffic off the wire and out of the UX log.;
#X text 30 150 How. The GUI sends /grab <address> 1 on pointerdown and /grab <address> 0 on pointerup or pointercancel. Those arrive here through formuls-osc-in \, the same receive the rest of the GUI's messages use. A grabbed address goes into one of four slots \, round robin \; outgoing packets whose address sits in an open slot are dropped. Ten slots \, because ten is the most fingers a tablet reports and a sweep across the panel with both hands is a real gesture on this instrument -- the logged sessions only ever showed two at once \, which is not a reason to design for two. Past ten it degrades rather than breaks: the longest-held address loses its slot and starts being echoed again \, which is the behaviour from before this abstraction existed. Reusing a live slot runs that slot's clear path first \, so depth stays equal to the number of slots actually held and the fast path still shuts when the last finger lifts. Releases are explicit rather than inferred from a timer \, because a timer would also swallow the correcting echo the patch sends when it clamps a value -- the one echo that has to arrive.;
#X text 30 262 Cost. While nothing is grabbed \, depth is 0 \, the parse branch is shut and a packet passes through one spigot. Only while a finger is down does each outgoing packet get its address read back out with [oscparse]. A global reset sends thousands of packets and happens with nothing touched \, so it keeps its old speed.;
#X text 30 330 In plain Pd nothing sends /grab \, so depth stays 0 and this is a wire.;
